                <div class="art-caption"><span>✳</span> The world is our classroom.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-bottom"><span>01 — START WITH A QUESTION</span><span>SCROLL TO EXPLORE ↓</span><span>22°21'58.4"N&nbsp; 91°49'32.0"E</span></div>
        </section>
        <section class="ticker" aria-label="Our approach"><div class="ticker-track"><span>LESS MEMORIZING</span><b>✳</b><span>MORE MAKING</span><b>✳</b><span>BIG QUESTIONS</span><b>✳</b><span>HANDS-ON SCIENCE</span><b>✳</b><span>LESS MEMORIZING</span><b>✳</b><span>MORE MAKING</span><b>✳</b><span>BIG QUESTIONS</span><b>✳</b><span>HANDS-ON SCIENCE</span><b>✳</b></div></section>
        <section id="story" class="story section-wrap section-pad">
            <div class="section-kicker"><span>01 / THE REASON WE’RE HERE</span><span class="kicker-line"></span><span>EST. 2025 · CHATTOGRAM</span></div>
            <div class="story-grid"><div><h2>Every great idea<br>starts with <em>“why?”</em></h2><div class="story-aside"><span class="asterisk">✳</span><p>We believe the next generation doesn’t need more answers handed to them. They need the tools, confidence, and space to find their own.</p></div></div><div class="story-copy"><p>Genius ZOO began with a simple thought: what if learning science felt less like memorizing facts and more like discovering something for the first time?</p><p>Our team spent years imagining a place where curious kids could tinker with real ideas, connect the dots between subjects, and turn “I wonder…” into “I made this.” In 2025, that place opened its doors in Chattogram.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://geniuszoo.com/about">More about our story <span>↗</span></a></div></div>
            <div class="stats-row"><div><strong>2013</strong><span>The first big idea</span></div><div><strong>2025</strong><span>Doors open in Chattogram</span></div><div><strong>4–16</strong><span>Ages we learn alongside</span></div><div class="stats-note">A decade of dreaming.<br>A lifetime of asking why.</div></div>
        </section>
        <section id="subjects" class="subjects-section section-pad"><div class="section-wrap"><div class="section-kicker"><span>02 / THE BUILDING BLOCKS</span><span class="kicker-line"></span><span>FOUR WAYS TO SEE THE WORLD</span></div><div class="subjects-heading"><h2>Not just subjects.<br><em>Superpowers.</em></h2><p>The best discoveries happen when ideas bump into each other. Our integrated STEM curriculum lets them connect the dots.</p></div><div class="subject-grid">
            <article class="subject-card science"><div class="card-top"><span>01 / NOTICE</span><span class="card-icon">◉</span></div><div class="subject-emoji">🧪</div><h3>Science</h3><p>Look closer. Ask why. Find out what happens next.</p><span class="card-foot">EXPERIMENT · OBSERVE · DISCOVER</span></article>
            <article class="subject-card technology"><div class="card-top"><span>02 / IMAGINE</span><span class="card-icon">↗</span></div><div class="subject-emoji">⌘</div><h3>Technology</h3><p>Turn “what if?” into something you can see, use, and share.</p><span class="card-foot">CODE · DESIGN · CREATE</span></article>
            <article class="subject-card engineering"><div class="card-top"><span>03 / MAKE</span><span class="card-icon">⚙</span></div><div class="subject-emoji">🛠️</div><h3>Engineering</h3><p>Dream up a solution. Build it. Make it even better.</p><span class="card-foot">TINKER · BUILD · IMPROVE</span></article>
            <article class="subject-card math"><div class="card-top"><span>04 / CONNECT</span><span class="card-icon">∑</span></div><div class="subject-emoji">⌗</div><h3>Mathematics</h3><p>Spot the patterns hiding in the things all around us.</p><span class="card-foot">NOTICE · REASON · SOLVE</span></article>
        </div></div></section>
        <section id="lab" class="lab-section section-pad"><div class="section-wrap"><div class="section-kicker"><span>03 / A LITTLE SOMETHING TO TRY</span><span class="kicker-line"></span><span>THE MINI LAB</span></div><div class="lab-intro"><h2>Curiosity, meet<br><em>your playground.</em></h2><p>Go ahead, press things. The best way to learn is to see what happens.</p></div><div class="lab-grid"><article class="lab-card formula-card"><div class="lab-card-head"><span>THE QUICK THINKER</span><span>LAB NOTE Nº 001</span></div><h3>How much energy<br>is hiding in here?</h3><p>A tiny bit of mass holds a wildly big amount of energy. Try it.</p><label for="massInput">Mass in kilograms</label><div class="input-row"><input id="massInput" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="1"><span>kg</span><button id="energyButton" aria-label="Calculate energy">↗</button></div><div class="formula-result" id="energyResult" aria-live="polite">E = mc² <span>· Give it a try</span></div><div class="formula-foot">E = mc²&nbsp;&nbsp; / &nbsp;&nbsp;c = 299,792,458 m/s</div></article>
            <article class="lab-card periodic-card"><div class="lab-card-head"><span>THE ELEMENTS, UP CLOSE</span><span>LAB NOTE Nº 002</span></div><h3>Meet the<br>building blocks.</h3><p>Pick an element. Every one tells a story.</p><div class="element-grid" id="elementGrid"><button data-name="Hydrogen" data-fact="The lightest and most abundant element in the universe."><small>1</small>H</button><button data-name="Helium" data-fact="So light it can lift a balloon, and it keeps stars shining."><small>2</small>He</button><button data-name="Lithium" data-fact="A soft metal that helps power the batteries in our everyday devices."><small>3</small>Li</button><button data-name="Carbon" data-fact="The versatile backbone of life, from diamonds to DNA."><small>6</small>C</button><button data-name="Nitrogen" data-fact="About 78% of the air around us is nitrogen."><small>7</small>N</button><button data-name="Oxygen" data-fact="A reactive gas that most living things need to breathe."><small>8</small>O</button><button data-name="Neon" data-fact="Pass an electric current through neon and it glows orange-red."><small>10</small>Ne</button><button data-name="Sodium" data-fact="A reactive metal that combines with chlorine to make table salt."><small>11</small>Na</button><button data-name="Iron" data-fact="Earth’s core is thought to be made mostly of iron and nickel."><small>26</small>Fe</button><button data-name="Gold" data-fact="One of the few metals found in nature in its pure form."><small>79</small>Au</button></div><div class="element-info" id="elementInfo" aria-live="polite">← Pick one to explore</div></article></div></div></section>
        <section class="promise section-pad"><div class="section-wrap promise-inner"><div class="promise-stamp">LEARN<br>BY DOING<br><span>✳</span></div><div><div class="section-kicker"><span>04 / A DIFFERENT KIND OF CLASSROOM</span></div><h2>Learning should<br>feel like <em>an adventure.</em></h2><p>Good questions. Messy experiments. That spark when something finally clicks. We make room for all of it — because that’s where the real learning happens.</p><a class="button button-light" href="https://geniuszoo.com/grade">Let’s get curious <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="promise-doodle">↗<br><span>There’s no<br>one way to<br>figure it out.</span></div></div></section>
        <section class="topics-section section-pad"><div class="section-wrap"><div class="section-kicker"><span>05 / FOLLOW THAT QUESTION</span><span class="kicker-line"></span><span>THERE’S ALWAYS MORE TO EXPLORE</span></div><div class="topics-heading"><h2>Where might<br><em>“what if?”</em> take you?</h2><div class="topic-arrows"><button id="topicPrev" aria-label="Previous topics">←</button><button id="topicNext" aria-label="Next topics">→</button></div></div><div class="topic-track" id="topicTrack"><article class="topic-card"><span>01 / SPACE</span><b>🌌</b><h3>How big<br>is the universe?</h3><p>Stars, planets, black holes, and the space in between.</p><span class="topic-arrow">↗</span></article><article class="topic-card"><span>02 / LIVING THINGS</span><b>🧬</b><h3>What makes<br>life tick?</h3><p>Zoom in on cells, DNA, and the science of being alive.</p><span class="topic-arrow">↗</span></article><article class="topic-card"><span>03 / ROBOTICS</span><b>🤖</b><h3>Can machines<br>learn to think?</h3><p>Meet the ideas shaping the future of robotics and AI.</p><span class="topic-arrow">↗</span></article><article class="topic-card"><span>04 / EVERYDAY PHYSICS</span><b>⚡</b><h3>Where does<br>the energy go?</h3><p>Find the invisible forces at work all around us.</p><span class="topic-arrow">↗</span></article><article class="topic-card"><span>05 / PATTERNS</span><b>⌗</b><h3>Are there<br>patterns in nature?</h3><p>From a nautilus shell to a spiral galaxy, math is everywhere.</p><span class="topic-arrow">↗</span></article></div></div></section>
        <section class="cta-section section-pad" id="contact"><div class="section-wrap cta-inner"><span class="cta-spark">✳</span><div class="section-kicker"><span>06 / THEIR NEXT BIG QUESTION STARTS HERE</span></div><h2>Ready to see<br>where <em>curiosity goes?</em></h2><p>Come say hello. We’d love to show you around.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="https://geniuszoo.com/grade">Explore classes <span>↗</span></a><div class="cta-orbit">GZ<br>✳</div></div></section>
